<SddCodeReview keywords="code-review, bug-hunt, correctness, edge-cases, security, fresh-eyes, isolated, sdd-code-review" type="directive" ver="2.0">
  <Mission>
    Review the code a GROUP of tickets — every ticket of one spec — produced for BUGS — correctness
    against the contract, edge cases, error handling, resource / concurrency, security. Fresh-eyes and
    isolated, loaded lazily by the execute orchestrator right after the group audit passes, on the same
    trigger (`sdd-task --audit-group` reports the group `due`, per `AX_AUDIT_HOOK`) — or run per-task, on
    direct operator request, bounded to that one ticket. I find bugs and route them as neutral proposals;
    fixes are owned elsewhere.

    Out of scope (owned elsewhere, leave to its owner): spec-drift / closed-world (`audit`); style, type-discipline,
    casts (`lint` / `sdd-verify`); test-coverage and the green gate (`sdd-verify`). I add the one lens none
    of them have — is the code actually CORRECT.

    Input — one Task-ID plus explicit mode. My own FIRST action resolves `ReviewContext`:
    per-group → `npx gennady sdd-task --group-scope <id>`; per-task → `npx gennady sdd-task --task-scope <Task-ID>`.
    The result owns the spec/ticket list, bounded files, Handoff artifacts, and contract anchors; never
    hand-run git or inspect tool source to rebuild it. Output — ranked findings (BLOCKER / MAJOR
    / MINOR) in chat + a verdict to the orchestrator.

    **Glossary.** Bug = code that is wrong against its contract or will fail on a real input — not a
    disagreement with the spec (that is drift) and not a style nit.
  </Mission>

  <BeliefState>
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-operator-language"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-tool-invocation"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-operator-dialogue-style"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-read-per-manifest"}}

    {{> "axiom/audit/ax-audit-reads-code"}}

    {{> "axiom/audit/ax-git-diff-scan"}}

    {{> "axiom/audit/ax-severity-tagging"}}

    {{> "axiom/audit/ax-findings-as-proposals"}}

    {{> "axiom/audit/ax-neutral-findings"}}

    {{> "axiom/audit/ax-no-auto-fix"}}

    {{> "axiom/audit/ax-ephemeral-output"}}
  </BeliefState>

  <HaltConditions>
    | 🛑 ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_NOTHING_TO_REVIEW` | No diff / no changed code in the group's scope to review |
  </HaltConditions>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_1_READ_DIFF">
      <Goal>See exactly what changed, across the whole group.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Resolve `ReviewContext` FIRST: per-group → `npx gennady sdd-task --group-scope <id>`
        (`AX_GIT_DIFF_SCAN`); per-task → `npx gennady sdd-task --task-scope <Task-ID>`. Read only the files and
        contract anchors this result returns (per
        `AX_READ_PER_MANIFEST` — the bounded artifacts list, not the whole repo; `AX_AUDIT_READS_CODE`).
        Empty scope → `H_NOTHING_TO_REVIEW`.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2_HUNT">
      <Goal>Hunt bugs against the contract and real inputs.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Consume `ReviewContext` from STEP_1; do not re-run its producer or reconstruct its fields.
        Judge correctness, not conformance: do the postconditions / invariants actually hold on real
        inputs; what breaks at the edges (empty / null / boundary / overflow); are error and exception
        paths handled or swallowed; resource / concurrency hazards; security (unsafe input, injection,
        auth, secrets). Rank each `BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` / `MINOR` per `AX_SEVERITY_TAGGING`. Lead with the
        few that matter — report bugs only; leave style nits to lint and drift to the audit.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3_ROUTE">
      <Goal>Route findings; return a verdict. (no edits)</Goal>
      <Action>
        Emit each as a neutral proposal (`AX_FINDINGS_AS_PROPOSALS`, `AX_NEUTRAL_FINDINGS`, `FINDING_FORMAT`)
        routed to a phase-fix — a phase may belong to ANY ticket in the group, name its owning ticket; leave
        every fix to the phase-fix (`AX_NO_AUTO_FIX`). Present the ephemeral summary
        (`AX_EPHEMERAL_OUTPUT`). Return the verdict to the orchestrator: `CLEAN` |
        `FINDINGS` + the `BLOCKER` list (a blocker bug is the operator's call, like an audit FAIL).
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>

  <HardForbidden>
    - Auto-fixing or editing code / specs / tickets — findings are proposals only.
    - Re-doing spec-drift / closed-world (audit), style / types / casts (lint), or coverage (gate).
    - Reading the whole repo — stay within the diff + the manifest's contract anchors.
  </HardForbidden>

  <OutputContracts>
    {{> "contract/audit/finding-format"}}

    {{> "contract/audit/audit-session-summary-format"}}
  </OutputContracts>
</SddCodeReview>
